purposes.content:
We use your personal information to:

• create and manage your account and authenticate your sign-ins;
• process, ship and support your orders, including transactional emails such as order confirmations;
• operate the loyalty program and apply your rewards;
• publish the reviews you choose to share;
• send you our newsletter and promotional emails when you have consented to receive them, in accordance with Canada's Anti-Spam Legislation (CASL), with an unsubscribe link in every message;
• prevent fraud, keep the platform secure and meet our legal obligations.

We do not sell your personal information, and we do not use it to make automated decisions that produce legal or similarly significant effects.

rights.content:
Subject to applicable law (Law 25 and PIPEDA in Canada, the GDPR in the European Economic Area), you have the right to:

• access the personal information we hold about you;
• rectify inaccurate or incomplete information;
• request deletion of your information, including by deleting your account from your profile;
• receive the information you provided to us in a structured, commonly used technological format (portability);
• withdraw your consent at any time, for example by unsubscribing from our emails or updating your email preferences;
• object to, or request the restriction of, certain processing where the GDPR applies.

To exercise any of these rights, write to privacy@blessp.com. We respond within 30 days. If you are not satisfied with our answer, you may file a complaint with the Commission d'accès à l'information du Québec (CAI), the Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada (OPC) or, if you are in the European Union, your local supervisory authority.

cookies.content:
We use a small set of cookies and browser storage entries, none of which are advertising trackers:

• essential authentication cookies that keep you securely signed in;
• your language and display currency preferences;
• your cookie-consent choice, your product comparison list, your recently viewed items and the dismissal of one-time messages such as the welcome offer.

When you first visit the site, a consent banner lets you accept or reject non-essential storage. You can also clear these entries at any time through your browser settings.
